          %title Selected writings
          %blockquote
            %p
              Not to be confused with John A. G. Roberts, working in
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dynamical+systems"} dynamical systems
          %p
            John Elias Roberts was a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+physicist"} mathematical physicist
            working on the mathematical foundations of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            in terms of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AQFT"} AQFT
          %p He was born in England, but his father came from the Llŷn Peninsula. He worked in Rome at Tor Vergata for a long time, before living his last few years in Goettingen.
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                cv:
                %a{:href => "https://www.mat.uniroma2.it/~dott/roberts.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://www.mathgenealogy.org/id.php?id=139019"} MathGenealogy page
          %h2#selected_writings Selected writings
          %p
            John Roberts wrote his PhD thesis on the notion of
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rigged+Hilbert+spaces"} rigged Hilbert spaces
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac"} Dirac
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+mechanics"} quantum mechanics
            precise. After that he followed the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haag-Kastler+axioms"} Haag-Kastler approach
            for axiomatizing quantum theory and became one of its central proponents.
          %p Early on he suggested in
          %ul
            %li#Roberts79
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+E.+Roberts"}> John E. Roberts
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Mathematical Aspects of Local Cohomology
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algèbres d’opérateurs et leurs applications en physique mathématique
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 274
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://dmitripavlov.org/scans/roberts-mathematical-aspects-of-local-cohomology.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Roberts-LocalCohomology.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+nets"} local nets
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+observables"} quantum observables
            (as formulated in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+quantum+field+theory"} algebraic quantum field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            – or rather of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            – with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-category"} ∞-category
          %p
            Motivated by this he was one of the first to consider a notion of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+%E2%88%9E-categories"} strict ∞-categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjecture"} conjectured
            that these are characterized by their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-nerves"} ∞-nerves
            being
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complicial+sets"} complicial sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"} Ross Street
            to develop the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientals"} orientals
            and to formulate a precise version of this conjecture, which was proven by
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dominic+Verity"} Dominic Verity
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ross+Street"}> Ross Street
              , pages 9-10 of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em An Australian conspectus of higher category theory
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                \-Categories: Foundations and Applications
              at the University of Minnesota (Minneapolis, 7–18 June 2004), in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Towards+Higher+Categories"} Towards Higher Categories
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 152
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uchicago.edu/~may/IMA/Street.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Street-Conspectus.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4419-1524-5"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4419-1524-5
          %p
            Later Roberts proved together with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Doplicher"} Doplicher
            what is now one of the central results in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AQFT"} AQFT
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Doplicher-Roberts+reconstruction+theorem"} Doplicher-Roberts reconstruction theorem
            – a version of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tannaka+duality"} Tannaka duality
            – which in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AQFT"} AQFT
            serves to intrinsically characterize the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superselection+sector"} superselection sector
          %p
            Introducing what came to be called
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/DHR+superselection+theory"} DHR superselection theory
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+quantum+field+theory"} algebraic quantum field theory
            (and the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Doplicher-Roberts+reconstruction+theorem"} Doplicher-Roberts reconstruction theorem
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergio+Doplicher"}> Sergio Doplicher
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rudolf+Haag"} Rudolf Haag
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+E.+Roberts"} John E. Roberts
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fields, observables and gauge transformations I
                %strong 13
                (1969) 1–23 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01645267"}> doi:10.1007/BF01645267
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergio+Doplicher"}> Sergio Doplicher
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rudolf+Haag"} Rudolf Haag
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+E.+Roberts"} John E. Roberts
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fields, observables and gauge transformations II
                %strong 15
                (1969) 173–200 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01645674"}> doi:10.1007/BF01645674
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            and relating to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/particle+statistics"} particle statistics
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parastatistics"}> parastatistics
            ) in view of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+locality"} causal locality
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergio+Doplicher"}> Sergio Doplicher
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rudolf+Haag"} Rudolf Haag
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+E.+Roberts"} John E. Roberts
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Local observables and particle statistics I
                %strong 23
                (1971) 199–230 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01877742"}> doi:10.1007/BF01877742
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/communications-in-mathematical-physics/volume-23/issue-3/Local-observables-and-particle-statistics-I/cmp/1103857630.full"} euclid:cmp/1103857630
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergio+Doplicher"}> Sergio Doplicher
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rudolf+Haag"} Rudolf Haag
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+E.+Roberts"} John E. Roberts
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Local observables and particle statistics I
                %strong 35
                (1974) 49–85 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01646454"}> doi:10.1007/BF01646454
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            More on
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superselection+sectors"} superselection sectors
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+E.+Roberts"}> John E. Roberts
              , p. 110 (5 of 14) in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Local cohomology and superselection structure
              %strong 51
              2 (1976) 107-119 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/communications-in-mathematical-physics/volume-51/issue-2/Local-cohomology-and-superselection-structure/cmp/1103900345.full"}> euclid:cmp/1103900345
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C-star+category"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
